WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.570
Hi, I'm Harshawardhan Chitnis, a software
development and AI and machine learning engineer.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.420
I have one year of professional
experience at Tata Consultancy Services,

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.870
where I worked on enterprise software systems and gained
hands-on experience with real-world application.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.320
I'm currently pursuing an ePostgraduate
Diploma in Computer Science and Artificial

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.450
Intelligence from IIT Bombay,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.470
further strengthening my foundation
across computer science,

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.480
artificial intelligence and machine learning.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.970
I enjoy turning real-world
problems into practical,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.670
intelligent and reliable software solutions.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.190
Let me walk you through some of
the projects I've built.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.770
First is ChalkBox,

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.010
an AI-powered lesson planning and classroom
assistant designed for teachers.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.060
It combines structured lesson generation
workflows with retrieval augmented

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.300
generation to create classroom-ready,
source-grounded teaching content from

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.730
textbooks and topics.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.110
The platform can generate board plans,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.440
classroom activities,

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.380
assessments,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.700
flashcards, quick teaching material and
presentation-ready outputs while maintaining

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.110
grounding to the original learning material.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.850
Next is Nivaran AI,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.770
an AI-led assistant designed for
e-commerce refund complaints.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.650
Users can upload supporting
documents and correspondence,

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.850
after which the system builds a
source-linked fact sheet,

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.420
identifies missing or conflicting information and
helps determine the appropriate next step.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:22.500
It can then prepare a structured complaint
pack while keeping important claims

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.030
connected to their original supporting evidence.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.110
Next is HealthNexus AI,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.250
a healthcare resilience and
resource management platform.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.330
It brings together demand forecasting,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.360
emergency simulation, early warnings and
intelligent resource redistribution to help

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.870
operators understand pressure before
shortages become critical.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:46.360
The India demonstration covers 207 fictional
healthcare facilities across all 36

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.660
states and union territories.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.850
It supports one-day, seven-day and
fourteen-day forecasting,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.960
emergency simulations for different
disruption scenarios and advisory resource

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:01.450
redistribution using optimization algorithms while
protecting donor facilities from new shortages.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.490
Next is the Electricity Bill Management System,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.910
a full-stack application built
using Spring Boot and Angular.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.350
It supports customer management,
bill generation and tracking,

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.720
payments, downloadable bills, complaint
handling and administrative operations

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.810
through a responsive web interface.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:22.380
The project also gave me practical
experience building secure REST APIs and

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.110
structured backend services for
complete end-to-end workflows.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.710
Next is Smart Parking Intelligence,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.320
a computer vision-based system designed to
determine parking space occupancy from

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.390
images and pre-recorded video.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.700
The system analyzes individual parking
spaces and identifies whether they are

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.840
occupied or vacant.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:45.450
It combines computer vision, machine
learning, parking slot geometry,

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:50.440
historical occupancy data, analytics and
reporting to create a complete parking

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.910
intelligence workflow rather than
simply detecting vehicles.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.220
Finally,

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:00.060
Privacy Aware Face Analytics is an end-to-end
computer vision platform for real-time

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.910
multi-face detection, tracking
and behavioral analytics.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.520
Privacy preserving anonymisation is integrated
directly into the inference pipeline.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.950
The project also covers the
machine learning lifecycle,

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.490
model experimentation and versioning,
containerized training and inference services,

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:17.700
backend APIs,

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:23.410
persistent analytics storage and dashboards for
visualizing both live and historical insights.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:28.760
Together, these projects reflect the areas I
enjoy working across most – artificial

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.870
intelligence, machine learning, computer vision,

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.630
full-stack development and building technology
around meaningful real-world problems.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.450
Thanks for exploring my work.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.450
You can discover each of these projects in
more detail throughout my portfolio.
